'`. Then replace the serialized-payload test with a walk over the event's entries and their nested `hooks` arrays that collects each `command` of an entry whose `type` is `command`, and report `ok` only when one matches `node` followed by whitespace and a path ending in the runtime's marker. Rewrite the comment above `eventPayload` to say a mention is not a wired hook, so only a command that runs the script counts. Verify: before the change both cases fail, after it `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` and `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and exits 0.\n\n  Line 164: - [ ] T064 Count a hook as wired only when `node` stands where a shell starts a command (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add three cases built with `writeClaudeSettings`, each with a `UserPromptSubmit` group holding one `{ type: 'command', command: <cmd> }` hook. With `node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` the check prints `ok claude` and exits 0. With `/opt/homebrew/bin/node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` it prints `ok claude` and exits 0. With `echo node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` it prints `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` and exits 1. Today the first passes, the second fails on `hook-missing` and the third fails on `ok claude`. Then rewrite `runsMarker`. A token, after `stripQuotes`, is a `node` executable when it equals `node` or ends with `/node`. It counts only at a command position: the first token of the command, a token right after `&&`, `||`, `;` or `|`, or the token right after `-c` when the token before `-c` is `bash` or `sh`. Report a match when such a token is followed by a token ending in the runtime's marker. These positions cover every real shape in this repository: `.cursor/hooks.json` starts its command with `node`, and `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json` and `.devin/hooks.v1.json` run `bash -c 'cd \"...\" && node <marker> || ...'`. Add a comment above `runsMarker` saying an argument that only names `node`, as `echo node <script>` does, runs nothing, so `node` must stand where a shell starts a command. Verify: before the change `NT $HWT` reports `fail 2`, after it `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0`, and `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and exits 0.\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":4,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 4 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:\n  Line 37: - WG6: `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n\n  Line 119: - [x] T029 Refuse a flag value that is another flag (`CK`, `CKT`). Test first: in `CKT`, add a case running `node $CK --root --json`: expect exit 2. Today it prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exits 0. Then make `parseArgs` return `null` when the value after `--root` or `--config` starts with `-`, as `HW` does. Verify: before the change the case fails on exit 0, after it `NT $CKT` reports `fail 0`.\n\n  Line 121: - [x] T031 Count a hook as wired only when a command runs it (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add two cases: a `.claude/settings.json` whose `UserPromptSubmit` group holds `{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\" }`, and one whose entry names the script only in a `description` field. Both print `ok claude` today and must print `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json`. Keep the wired case passing with the real shape `bash -c 'cd \"$PWD\" && node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js'`. Then replace the serialized-payload test with a walk over the event's entries and their nested `hooks` arrays that collects each `command` of an entry whose `type` is `command`, and report `ok` only when one matches `node` followed